L458: We are seeking your participation (or that of your family member) in a research study
L459: because you (or your family member) have been admitted to an intensive care unit and
L460: are treated for a serious infection. However, before you agree to participate, please take
L461: the time to read, understand and carefully consider the following information. If you
L462: agree to take part in this research study, you will be asked to sign the consent form at
L463: the end of this document and we will give you a signed copy for your own records.
L464: This Information and Consent Form explains the goals, procedures, risks,
L465: inconveniences and benefits of the study as well as providing the names of the people
L466: to reach if needed. This document may contain information or words that you do not
L467: understand. Please ask the study investigator or members of the study staff to answer
L468: your questions and explain any word or information you do not understand.
L469: **Version 4: October 2** ~~**[nd]**~~ **, 2019** **Page 1 of 10**
L470: **Lessening organ dysfunction with vitamin C: LOVIT Trial**
L471: **NATURE AND GOALS OF THE RESEARCH STUDY**
L472: This study aims to determine whether the administration of vitamin C in patients
L473: admitted to an intensive care unit (ICU) with a serious infection improves their health
L474: status. The current options to treat infections are limited to antibiotics and supportive
L475: care for bodily functions (like hydration fluids in the veins, medication to maintain blood
L476: pressure, mechanical ventilation and treatment to ensure kidney function). Recent
L477: studies suggest that high doses of vitamin C given into veins may be the first therapy
L478: helping the body to fight serious infections.
L479: The goal of this study is to determine if the administration of vitamin C decreases the
L480: harmful effects of the infection on organs and improves your health status more rapidly
L481: than placebo. The specific objectives are to evaluate the effects of vitamin C on your
L482: health status and quality of life at 6 months and on blood levels of biomarkers that
L483: reflect cellular health. We wish to include approximately 100 participants at the _CIUSSS_
L484: _de l’Estrie - CHUS_ to be among the 800 participants needed for this study that will be
L485: carried out in 25 hospital centers in Canada. This study will be conducted over 4 years.
L486: Our research team has determined that you are eligible to participate in our study, and
L487: your treating physician agrees.
L488: **RESEARCH STUDY PROCEDURES**
L489: If you agree to participate in this study, you or your family member, will be assigned to
L490: either the group to whom we administer vitamin C or to the group to whom we
L491: administer a placebo (an inactive substance that has the same appearance that the
L492: study product) in the veins. Your assignment to one of these two groups will be
L493: determined randomly by a computer that will not retain information about you. The
L494: probability of being assigned to either group is 50% (1 in 2 chances or half-and-half).
L495: The treating team will not be aware of the group to which you have been assigned, but
L496: the doctor in charge of this study can obtain this information rapidly in case of
L497: emergency.
L498: As a study participant, you will receive the study product (vitamin C or placebo) 4 times
L499: per day during 96 hours or up to your discharge from the intensive care unit whichever
L500: comes first. Also, on days 1, 3 and 7 of participation (or when you are discharged from
L501: the intensive care unit if it happens before day 7), the nurse will collect 10 ml of urine (2
L502: teaspoons) and 25 ml of blood (5 teaspoons) samples while taking the blood samples
L503: required for your regular medical care. We will collect a little more volume than what is
L504: needed to compensate for unexpected losses that may arise during laboratory testing.
L505: These samples will enable us to measure certain biomarkers in your blood that help
L506: assess the function of body’s cells and organ systems.
L507: During your hospital stay, we will monitor your progress to see if your organs are
L508: functioning well and if you develop other health problems, and to see how long you stay
L509: in the ICU and hospital. Your medical chart will be reviewed by the investigator and the
L510: research team as long as you remain in the study. Blood test results and procedures
L511: present in your medical record will be collected for the study.
L512: **Version 4: October 2** ~~**[nd]**~~ **, 2019** **Page 2 of 10**
L513: **Lessening organ dysfunction with vitamin C: LOVIT Trial**
L514: After you are discharged from the hospital, you will be contacted by telephone 6 months
L515: after the start of your participation in the study. Your contact information will be provided
L516: to the Study Coordinating Centre located at the Centre de recherche du Centre
L517: hospitalier universitaire de Sherbrooke.
L518: **FUTURE ANALYSES**
L519: Once the biomarker analyses have been performed as part of this study, it is possible
L520: that parts of your samples haven’t been used. We wish to use the remainder of your
L521: samples to answer additional questions concerning the impact of vitamin C that may
L522: arise in future. For example, we may measure a new, as yet undefined, biomarker. Only
L523: the remainder of your samples will be used and no other additional sample will be
L524: collected.
L525: **RISKS ASSOCIATED WITH PARTICIPATION IN THIS RESEARCH STUDY**
L526: Vitamin C is generally not toxic. Risks associated to vitamin C are nausea, vomiting,
L527: abdominal cramps, tiredness, hot flashes, headaches, insomnia, drowsiness and
L528: diarrhea. When vitamin C is administered too rapidly, there is a risk of weakness and
L529: dizziness. There is very little probability that these happen since vitamin C will be
L530: administered on a 30 to 60 minutes period each time a dose is given. There is a
L531: possibility of developing a clot in a deep vein but the simple fact of lying in bed for a
L532: long time can cause a clot.
L533: A potential risk is the formation of kidney stones. Vitamin C might increase, decrease or
L534: not affect the risk of kidney stones. Whatever the effect on the risk of kidney stones, you
L535: might not have symptom or a deterioration of your kidney function can occur, but be
L536: counter balanced by a decrease of global mortality. We will nonetheless monitor
L537: damage that could harm your kidneys.
L538: Vitamin C may be associated with an exaggerated destruction of red blood cells
L539: (hemolysis) in patients with G6PD enzyme deficiency. However, these patients are
L540: excluded from participating in the trial. Patients affected by G6PD deficiency are very
L541: rare in Canada comparatively to other countries in the world. If hemolysis happens to
L542: you during the intervention period, we will stop the study drug and provide standard
L543: supportive care.
L544: Vitamin C can give falsely high blood sugar results when it is measured with certain
L545: devices used at the bedside. This problem does not occur with equipment used in the
L546: hospital laboratory. If a falsely high blood sugar result from a bedside device occurred,
L547: your doctor may decide to use insulin to lower your blood sugar, which may cause low
L548: blood sugar (hypoglycaemia). In this study, various measures are taken to minimize the
L549: risk of false blood sugar levels, including the use of bedside devices that are more
L550: reliable than others, and more frequent blood tests for blood sugar to be measured in
L551: the hospital laboratory. Accordingly, this study may be associated with more frequent
L552: blood tests.
L553: **RISKS ASSOCIATED TO THE PROCEDURES**
L554: **Version 4: October 2** ~~**[nd]**~~ **, 2019** **Page 3 of 10**
L555: **Lessening organ dysfunction with vitamin C: LOVIT Trial**
L556: The risks associated to blood samples are the following: mild pain, dizziness, fainting,
L557: bruising, bleeding and in rare cases blood clots and infection. However, you or your
L558: family member will have already a catheter in place that allows for blood samples to be
L559: drawn without a puncture (and then not exposed to the risks mentioned above).
L560: **RISKS ASSOCIATED WITH PREGNANCY**
L561: Taking part in this research study may include known or unknown risks to pregnant
L562: women, embryos, foetuses, or breastfed infants. Therefore, pregnant or breastfeeding
L563: women cannot participate in this research study.
L564: **BENEFITS ASSOCIATED WITH YOUR PARTICIPATION IN THE RESEARCH STUDY**
L565: You might have a personal benefit to participate in this research study, but we can’t
L566: guarantee. However, the findings from this study may help increase our knowledge of
L567: infections and vitamin C administration, which may benefit future patients.
L568: **VOLUNTARY PARTICIPATION AND THE RIGHT TO WITHDRAW**
L569: Your participation in this research study is voluntary. Therefore, you may refuse to
L570: participate. You can also withdraw from the study at any time, without providing a
L571: reason, by informing the study investigator or one of his assistants.
L572: Your decision not to participate in the study or to withdraw from it will have no impact on
L573: the quality of care and services you are entitled to or on your relationship with the
L574: investigator and other stakeholders.
L575: The study investigator, the funding agency or the research ethics board may end your
L576: participation in the study. This may happen if new findings or information indicates that
L577: participation is no longer in your interest; if the study investigator believes it is in your
L578: best interest; or if there are administrative reasons to terminate the study.
L579: If you withdraw or are withdrawn from the study, the information and material already
L580: collected during the course of the study will be stored, analyzed or used to protect the
L581: scientific integrity of the study.
L582: Any new study findings that could influence your decision to stay in the research study
L583: will be shared with you as soon as possible.
L584: **CONFIDENTIALITY**
L585: While you take part in this research project, the study investigator and study staff will
L586: collect and record information about you in a study file. They will only collect information
L587: required to meet the scientific goals of the study.
L588: This study file may include information from your medical chart concerning your past
L589: and present health status, your lifestyle as well as the test results, exams and
L590: procedures you will undergo during the study.
L591: Study samples will be sent to the Centre de recherche du Centre hospitalier
L592: universitaire de Sherbrooke, under the responsibility of Dr. François Lamontagne, and
L593: kept until the end of the study and the analyses for this study exclusively and then
L594: destroyed.
L595: **Version 4: October 2** ~~**[nd]**~~ **, 2019** **Page 4 of 10**
L596: **Lessening organ dysfunction with vitamin C: LOVIT Trial**
L597: All the information collected during the study will remain strictly confidential to the extent
L598: provided by law. You will be identified by an alphanumeric code. The key to the code
L599: linking your name to your study file will be kept in a safe place by the doctor in charge of
L600: this research study.
L601: Your full name and your telephone number will be transmitted to a qualified person of
L602: the Study Coordinating Centre to allow this person to contact you in 6 months by
L603: telephone. We will also ask you (or your family member) the name and phone number
L604: of alternative contacts to ensure we facilitate the telephone follow-up in 6 months. This
L605: personal information will allow a direct identification. This information will be kept in
L606: security and confidentiality will be preserved by the qualified person of the Study
L607: Coordinating Centre and destroyed at the end of the follow-up.
L608: To ensure your safety, a mention of your participation in this research study will be
L609: included in your medical file. Therefore, any person or company to whom you will give
L610: access to your medical file will have access to this information.
L611: The doctor responsible of this study will send to the principal investigator of the study,
L612: the coded data concerning your participation.
L613: The research data will be stored by the study investigator for at least 25 years.
L614: Study results may be published in medical journals or discussed at scientific meetings,
L615: but it will be impossible to identify you.
L616: For monitoring and control purposes, your study file and medical records may be
L617: examined by a representative of the Research Ethics Board of the institution or by a
L618: person mandated by a regulatory authority, for example, Health Canada. Data from your
L619: study file will be sent to the Data Management Centre located within the Department of
L620: Health Research Methods, Evidence, and Impact at McMaster University. All these
L621: individuals and organizations adhere to confidentiality policies.
L622: You have the right to consult your study file at any time to verify the information
L623: gathered and to have it corrected, if necessary, for as long as this information is
L624: available to the study investigator or the institution. However, some of this information
L625: may be made available to you only once the study has ended, to protect the scientific
L626: integrity of the study.
L627: **COMPENSATION**
L628: You will not receive any compensation for expenses and inconveniences incurred due
L629: to your participation in this research study.
L630: **SHOULD YOU SUFFER ANY HARM**
L631: Should you suffer any harm due to your participation in this research study, you will be
L632: provided with all the necessary care and services, at no cost to you.
L633: By agreeing to take part in this study, you are not waiving any of your legal rights nor
L634: discharging the study investigators, the sponsor or the institution where this research
L635: study is being conducted of their civil liability and professional responsibilities.
L636: **CONTACT PERSONS**
