L763: LOVIT Authorship and Sub-Study Guidelines Confidential
L764: **1.0.** **INTRODUCTION**
L765: This document describes the policies for the protocol and primary manuscripts, substudies, and secondary analyses and manuscripts. The LOVIT Principal Investigators
L766: encourage co-investigators to develop ideas for sub-studies to be conducted alongside the
L767: LOVIT trial and to submit proposals for secondary analyses and corresponding
L768: manuscripts using the LOVIT data. Sub-studies are defined as studies that build on the
L769: LOVIT trial infrastructure and require additional data collection. Secondary analyses and
L770: manuscripts use data that are collected as part of the LOVIT trial to address a research
L771: question that is not included in the LOVIT protocol.
L772: **2.0 PROTOCOL MANUSCRIPT AND PRIMARY MANUSCRIPT**
L773: We will use named authorship (as opposed to group authorship) for the LOVIT protocol
L774: publication and primary LOVIT results publications ( **Figure 1** ). Under the direction of
L775: the Principal Investigators, the named co-authors will be responsible for the preparation
L776: of the manuscripts. The Executive Committee will collaboratively determine named coauthors based on the tool in **Table 1** . The Principal Investigators envision many named
L777: co-authors for both the protocol manuscript and the primary manuscript. To be a named
L778: co-author, individuals must also meet the ICMJE authorship requirements ( **Table 2** ).
L779: The order of authorship will be based on the level of contribution to the LOVIT trial, as
L780: determined by the Executive Committee, with support from the Steering Committee
L781: membership as needed. The tool in **Table 1** may also be used to determine authorship
L782: order.
L783: **Table 1: Tool for Determining Named Co-Authors and Authorship Order**
L784: |Item|Specify|Level of<br>Engagement or<br>Contribution|Comments|
L785: |---|---|---|---|
L786: |Leadership role(s) in trial|- Active member of the<br>Steering Committee<br>- Country lead<br>- Other committee<br>member role (specify)<br>- Coordinating Centre<br>role (specify)<br>- Other leadership role<br>(specify)|- Very high<br>- High<br>- Moderate<br>- Low<br>- Very low||
L787: |Clinical site leadership|- Patient enrolment<br>- Data quality<br>- Patient follow-up|- Very high<br>- High<br>- Moderate<br>- Low<br>- Very low||
L788: |Expertise provided|- Design<br>- Methodology<br>- Clinical<br>- Statistical<br>- Other (specify)|- Very high<br>- High<br>- Moderate<br>- Low<br>- Very low||
L789: 10-Oct-2018                    Page **3** of **11** Version 1.0
L790: LOVIT Authorship and Sub-Study Guidelines Confidential
L791: |Item|Specify|Level of<br>Engagement or<br>Contribution|Comments|
L792: |---|---|---|---|
L793: |Drafted sections of the<br>manuscript||- Very high<br>- High<br>- Moderate<br>- Low<br>- Very low||
L794: |Provided input on the<br>interpretation of the data||- Very high<br>- High<br>- Moderate<br>- Low<br>- Very low||
L795: |Critically reviewed and<br>edited the manuscript||- Very high<br>- High<br>- Moderate<br>- Low<br>- Very low||
L796: **Table 2: ICMJE Authorship Requirements (available at http://icmje.org/)**
L797: 1. Substantial contributions to the conception or design of the work; or the acquisition, analysis, or
L798: interpretation of data for the work; AND
L799: 2. Drafting the work or revising it critically for important intellectual content; AND
L800: 3. Final approval of the version to be published; AND
L801: 4. Agreement to be accountable for all aspects of the work in ensuring that questions related to the
L802: accuracy or integrity of any part of the work are appropriately investigated and resolved.
L803: In addition to being accountable for the parts of the work he or she has done, an author should be able to
L804: identify which co-authors are responsible for specific other parts of the work. In addition, authors should
L805: have confidence in the integrity of the contributions of their co-authors.
L806: The Principal Investigators will take the lead on preparing the first drafts of both the
L807: protocol manuscript and the primary manuscript. They will ask named co-authors to draft
L808: sections of the manuscripts, provide clinical or methodological expertise, and critically
L809: review the manuscripts in their entirety.
L810: For the protocol manuscript and the primary manuscripts, all members of the LOVIT
L811: team will be listed in the contributor appendix (see Section 5.0). Journal rules on listing
L812: contributors will be followed in an effort to ensure that all contributors are searchable
L813: through PubMed.
