L826: **3.0 SUB-STUDIES**
L827: LOVIT co-investigators may submit ideas for sub-studies that build on the existing
L828: infrastructure and data collected within the LOVIT trial. LOVIT co-investigators should
L829: submit proposals for sub-studies to the Principal Investigator(s) or Project Manager(s) at
L830: the Coordinating Centre. All ideas for sub-studies will be archived.
L831: The proposals should include:
L832:   - Background and rationale
L833:   - Research question(s)
L834:   - Methods
L835:   - Statistical analysis plan (if developed)
L836:   - Timeline
L837:   - Implementation plan
L838:   - Impact on the LOVIT trial
L839:   - Budget and sources of funding
L840: The Principal Investigators and Project Managers, with input from the Steering
L841: Committee and larger LOVIT team as needed, will determine which sub-studies will be
L842: accepted. To do so, the Principal Investigators will complete the tool in **Table 3** to help
L843: guide their decision. The Principal Investigators may also request members of the
L844: Steering Committee review the proposals and complete the below tool, as needed. As a
L845: general rule, sub-studies should not compromise the likelihood of successfully
L846: completing the main trial within set timelines.
L847: If multiple co-investigators submit the same (or similar) ideas for sub-studies, the
L848: Principal Investigator(s), with support from the Steering Committee as needed, will select
L849: 10-Oct-2018                    Page **5** of **11** Version 1.0
L850: LOVIT Authorship and Sub-Study Guidelines Confidential
L851: a co-investigator to take the lead on the sub-study. This selection will be based on
L852: knowledge of the topic proposed, availability of the required resources (e.g. coinvestigator time) to devote to the sub-study, and contributions to the LOVIT trial (e.g.
L853: Steering Committee member, volume of patients enrolled at clinical site, etc.). The
L854: checklist tool in **Table 3** may be used to guide this decision. Co-investigators who
L855: submitted similar ideas may be invited to contribute as co-investigators on the sub-study
L856: at the discretion of the Principal Investigators and the lead co-investigator. If a lead coinvestigator is unable to devote sufficient time and resources to a sub-study, the Principal
L857: Investigators, with guidance from the study team, may recommend that another coinvestigator lead the sub-study.
L858: **Table 3: Tool for Determining Which Sub-Studies to Approve**
L859: |Item|Strongly<br>Disagree|Disagree|Neutral|Agree|Strongly<br>Agree|Comments|
L860: |---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
L861: |Sub-study<br>addresses an<br>important,<br>clinically<br>relevant, and<br>timely research<br>question|||||||
L862: |Sub-study is<br>feasible and can<br>be completed|||||||
L863: |Sub-study will<br>have a positive<br>impact on the<br>LOVIT trial|||||||
L864: |There are<br>adequate funding<br>and resources to<br>complete the sub-<br>study|||||||
L865: |Co-investigator is<br>on the Steering<br>Committee<br>(Yes/No)|||||||
L866: |Co-investigator is<br>from a high<br>enrolling clinical<br>site|||||||
L867: |Data is of high<br>quality at the co-<br>investigator’s<br>clinical site|||||||
L868: |Co-investigator<br>actively<br>participates in<br>LOVIT trial<br>meetings|||||||
L869: 10-Oct-2018                    Page **6** of **11** Version 1.0
L870: LOVIT Authorship and Sub-Study Guidelines Confidential
L871: The Principal Investigators, and members of the Executive Committee (and Steering
L872: Committee as needed), will meet and review the sub-study proposals and their responses
L873: each of the above questions. They will collaboratively determine which proposals to
L874: accept via consensus. Once a decision has been made, the Principal Investigators will
L875: communicate the decision to the co-investigator who submitted the sub-study proposals.
L876: If a proposal is not accepted, a Principal Investigator may telephone the co-investigator to
L877: explain the rationale for not moving forward with the proposed sub-study.
L878: The Principal Investigators, the Project Managers at the Coordinating Centre, and
L879: members of the LOVIT team (as needed), will work with the co-investigators on accepted
L880: sub-study proposals to develop the sub-study protocol and incorporate it into the LOVIT
L881: trial infrastructure. They will also provide oversight and support, as needed, to the
L882: conduct of the sub-study.
L883: For sub-study LOVIT publications, we will typically credit authorship those who led and
L884: participated in the sub-study, with acknowledgment to the rest of the group, i.e., on
L885: behalf of the LOVIT Investigators ( **Figure 2)** . All named authors will be expected to
L886: adhere to ICMJE authorship criteria; it is anticipated that the LOVIT Principal
L887: Investigators will qualify for authorship. The tool found in **Table 1** may be used to for
L888: determining guide authorship and all authors must meet the criteria in **Table 2** . All other
L889: contributors will be listed in the contributor appendix and every effort will be made to
L890: ensure that all contributors are searchable through PubMed.
L891: **Sub-Study Manuscript Title**
L892: Author A, Author B, and Author C on behalf of the LOVIT Investigators
