L900: **4.0 SECONDARY ANALYSES AND MANUSCRIPTS**
L901: We encourage LOVIT co-investigators to conduct/oversee secondary analyses and to
L902: write the corresponding secondary manuscripts using the data that is collected within the
L903: LOVIT trial. LOVIT co-investigators should submit proposals for secondary analyses
L904: 10-Oct-2018                    Page **7** of **11** Version 1.0
L905: LOVIT Authorship and Sub-Study Guidelines Confidential
L906: and corresponding manuscripts to the Principal Investigators or Project Managers at the
L907: Coordinating Centre.
L908: The proposals should include:
L909:   - Background and rationale
L910:   - Research question(s)
L911:   - Proposed methods
L912:   - Statistical analysis plan (if developed)
L913:   - Timeline
L914:   - Requirement of Coordinating Centre resources (e.g. statistical analysis support)
L915:   - Funding / resources
L916: The Principal Investigators and Project Managers, with input from the Executive
L917: Committee and Steering Committee as needed, will review the proposal and determine if
L918: it is acceptable. They may use the checklist tool in **Table 4** to help make this
L919: determination. They may request additional details and clarification from the coinvestigator if the any aspect of the proposal is unclear. They may also request revisions
L920: to the proposal. The Principal Investigators may also deny a request for a secondary
L921: analysis, and if so, they will provide a rationale to the co-investigator who submitted it.
L922: If multiple co-investigators submit the same (or similar) ideas for secondary analyses and
L923: corresponding manuscripts, the Principal Investigator(s), with support from the Executive
L924: and Steering Committees as needed, will select a co-investigator to take the lead on the
L925: analysis and manuscript preparation. This selection will be based on: knowledge of the
L926: topic proposed, availability of the required resources (e.g. co-investigator time) to
L927: complete the secondary analysis and corresponding manuscript in a timely fashion, and
L928: contributions to the LOVIT trial (e.g. Steering Committee member, volume of patients
L929: enrolled at clinical site, etc.). The checklist tool in **Table 4** may be used to guide this
L930: decision. Co-investigators who submitted similar ideas may be invited to contribute as
L931: co-authors at the discretion of the Principal Investigators and the lead co-investigator. If
L932: a lead co-investigator is unable to complete the planned analyses and secondary paper in
L933: a timely fashion, the Principal Investigators, with guidance from the study team, may
L934: recommend that another co-investigator take the lead.
L935: **Table 4: Tool for Determining Which Secondary Analyses and Manuscripts to Approve**
L936: |Item|Strongly<br>Disagree|Disagree|Neutral|Agree|Strongly<br>Agree|Comments|
L937: |---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
L938: |Analyses<br>addresses an<br>important,<br>clinically<br>relevant, and<br>timely research<br>question|||||||
L939: |Analysis is<br>feasible and can<br>be completed|||||||
