L951: The LOVIT study statistician will work with the lead co-investigator and members of the
L952: study team to develop the statistical analysis plan. In most situations, the statistical
L953: analyses will be conducted by the LOVIT statistician. If the analysis is not conducted by
L954: the LOVIT statistician, the LOVIT Principal Investigators and statistician will review the
L955: statistical analysis plan. They will also determine which data fields to send to the coinvestigator for analysis.
L956: The Principal Investigators will also review draft manuscripts and they will approve the
L957: final manuscript prior to journal submission to ensure that the manuscript is of acceptable
L958: quality.
L959: The Principal Investigators may also ask members of the LOVIT co-investigators to lead
L960: LOVIT secondary analyses and manuscripts. This selection will be based on the
L961: knowledge and interest of a topic and contributions to LOVIT trial. The applicable
L962: processes, as described above, will be followed.
L963: 10-Oct-2018                    Page **9** of **11** Version 1.0
L964: LOVIT Authorship and Sub-Study Guidelines Confidential
L965: Coordinating Centre personnel may assist with the secondary analysis and manuscript
L966: preparation, as needed. The LOVIT Coordinating Centre Project Managers will maintain
L967: a listing of all secondary analyses and manuscripts including the lead co-investigator, coauthors, and the status of the analysis and manuscript. Additionally, the Principal
L968: Investigators, with input from the Steering Committee and Project Managers, may
L969: prioritize the order in which the secondary analyses are conducted. The Principal
L970: Investigators are responsible for ensuring the quality of the secondary manuscripts and
L971: that the messaging of the secondary manuscripts is not conflicting.
L972: For secondary LOVIT publications, we will credit authorship to the individual coinvestigators who write the secondary manuscripts, with acknowledgment to the rest of
L973: the group, i.e., on behalf of the LOVIT Investigators ( **Figure 3** ). The lead investigator for
L974: each secondary paper, with support from the Principal Investigators, will determine
L975: named co-authors. Named co-authors will include the Principal Investigators and
L976: members of the LOVIT team who actively contribute to the publication per ICMJE
L977: authorship criteria. The tool in **Table 1** may be used to for determining guide authorship
L978: and all authors must meet the criteria in **Table 2** . All other contributors will be listed in
L979: the contributor appendix and every effort will be made to ensure that all contributors are
L980: searchable through PubMed.
